  "detection": "Hints, not a limit. A hint with foundBy \"project\" is in use when the package declares one of its dependencies, holds one of its config files, or has a package script or CI step (.github/workflows, .gitlab-ci.yml) that matches its script pattern or uses one of its CI actions; a working tool fills its role, so another declared tool of that role plans no install. A hint with foundBy \"machine\" is present when one of its commands answers on PATH. hostTools are tools the active host reports (--host-tools). A category names the roles its review needs; any hint of that role and kind fills it. recommend names the hint to suggest only when nothing fills the role. A user-scope install with commands runs after the user's yes only when it marks sudo false and needs no licence or signIn; any other install is printed steps.",
